<title>USA: Jostens Inc Q2 Dec 28 net down, sales up.</title>
<headline>Jostens Inc Q2 Dec 28 net down, sales up.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			 $ 0.11		   $ 0.31</p>
<p> Net			  4,224		   11,973</p>
<p> Revs		     171,719		  165,779</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  38,664		   38,578</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q2 includes shift of about $0.11 a share in earnings to the company's July quarter due to a change in accounting for inventory and added reserves of $0.09 a share to cover an environmental investigation and clean-up.  </p>
<p>	  SIX MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr loss		  $ 0.02   profit     $  0.35</p>
<p> Net loss		     803   profit	14,486</p>
<p> Revs		     277,118		  263,533</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  38,660		   41,542</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Jostens said its financial statements reflect a previously announced plan to treat the July-December 1996 period as a transitional &quot;stub&quot; period as it changes from a July-June fiscal year to a January-December fiscal year. The company said the change will enable better business planning and management.</p>
<p>	    ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
